          {
            "type": "reasoning_text",
            "text": "The user asks me to explain the idea of binary search in one sentence, in Chinese.\n\nBinary search (二分查找): Compare the target with the middle element of a sorted array. If they match, done. If the target is smaller, search the left half; if larger, search the right half. Repeat until found or the search space is empty.\n\nOne sentence in Chinese: 二分查找是在有序数组中，每次将目标值与中间元素比较，从而将查找范围缩小一半，逐步逼近目标值。\n\nI should keep it to one sentence as requested. Keep it concise."
          }
        ],
        "encrypted_content": "The user asks me to explain the idea of binary search in one sentence, in Chinese.\n\nBinary search (二分查找): Compare the target with the middle element of a sorted array. If they match, done. If the target is smaller, search the left half; if larger, search the right half. Repeat until found or the search space is empty.\n\nOne sentence in Chinese: 二分查找是在有序数组中，每次将目标值与中间元素比较，从而将查找范围缩小一半，逐步逼近目标值。\n\nI should keep it to one sentence as requested. Keep it concise."
